<title>ISRAEL: Israel July economic performance index up 0.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Israel July economic performance index up 0.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's economic performance or &quot;S&quot; index rose 0.2 percent in July, the Bank of Israel said.</p>
<p>		    July 96    June 96    July 95</p>
<p>Month-on-month</p>
<p>change		+ 0.2	- 0.1	+ 0.4</p>
<p>index		 116.4	116.1	109.9</p>
<p>(base 100=1994)</p>
<p>The &quot;S&quot; index is made up of four components: retail sales, which rose 2.0 percent in July; imports, which rose 2.0 percent in July; the number of workers, which rose 0.3 percent in January; and industrial production, which rose 0.3 percent in May.</p>
<p>Note: figures for the number of workers and industrial production lag.</p>
